    [GB10][spec] Make EAGLE draft-extend cudagraph build decision unanimous across TP ranks
    
    The draft-extend cudagraph runner runs a collective tp_group.barrier() per
    batch size during capture, so it must be built on ALL TP ranks or NONE.
    
    On multi-node, single-GPU-per-node setups the per-rank draft-extend attention
    backend can resolve differently (it derives from a current-device capability
    probe), so one rank builds the runner and enters the collective barrier while
    the peer skips it and proceeds to the scheduler event loop -> permanent init
    deadlock (rank-0 idle in recv_requests broadcast, rank-1 blocked in
    _capture_init barrier).
    
    Reconcile the build decision with a logical-AND (all_gather_object on the TP
    cpu_group) so every rank builds the runner or none does. Observed on a 2-node
    GB10 (sm_121a) cluster serving Qwen3.6-27B (hybrid GDN) with NEXTN k=3.

